# Core PHP + Laravel-like folders

This repository is **core / plain PHP**, not a Laravel application.

## Do

- Keep a Laravel-**inspired** folder layout (`app/`, `bootstrap/`, `config/`, `database/`, `public/`, `resources/`, `routes/`, `storage/`)
- Put shared logic in `app/Support`, `app/Services`, and (when useful) thin files under `app/Http/Controllers`
- Keep the web document root in `public/`
- Use plain PHP, PDO, sessions, and the existing `public/api/*.php` endpoints

## Do not

- Do not install or assume Laravel, Artisan, Eloquent, Blade, Vite, or `composer create-project laravel/laravel`
- Do not rewrite the app into a Laravel framework unless the user explicitly asks
- Do not describe the project as “a Laravel app”

When adding features, extend the core PHP codebase inside this folder layout.
